{"id": "EUVD-2026-101217", "enisaUuid": "f37d1705-f543-38e6-8f5e-1bf499fbfbc5", "description": "OW2 ASM 3.0 before 9.11 contains an uncontrolled recursion vulnerability in SignatureReader.parseType() that allows attackers to exhaust the stack via deeply nested generic type signatures. Attackers can supply a crafted class file with a long Signature attribute containing many nested type arguments to trigger a StackOverflowError during class transformation, causing denial of service.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T14:16:34", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T16:12:42", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://gitlab.ow2.org/asm/asm/-/merge_requests/465", "https://gitlab.ow2.org/asm/asm/-/commit/8f87fc0317a4c5ee8f538bcbb641928def25dbd6", "https://gitlab.ow2.org/asm/asm/-/blob/ASM_9_10_1/asm/src/main/java/org/objectweb/asm/signature/SignatureReader.java#L151", "https://asm.ow2.io/versions.html", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/ow2-asm-3.0-before-9.11-uncontrolled-recursion-in-signaturereader"], "aliases": ["GHSA-9vfw-838x-23h7", "CVE-2026-110263"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1226d2a7-bebe-3132-a09e-9966974cf629", "product": {"name": "ASM", "vendor": {"name": "OW2"}}, "product_version": "3.0 <9.11"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "cbc5af72-6e7f-3030-bd13-50468e57ff48", "vendor": {"name": "OW2"}}], "isExploited": false}